  "question": {
    "text": "The square of the distance of the image of the point $(6,1,5)$ in the line $\\frac{x-1}{3}=\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{z-2}{4}$, from the origin is _________"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "62",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0036_ae73b81e61fe.png\"><br />Let $\\mathrm{M}(3 \\lambda+1,2 \\lambda, 4 \\lambda+2)$\n$\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{AM}} \\cdot \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}=0$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 9 \\lambda-15+4 \\lambda-2+16 \\lambda-12=0$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 29 \\lambda=29$\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\lambda=1$\n$\\mathrm{M}(4,2,6), \\mathrm{I}=(2,3,7)$\nRequired Distance $=\\sqrt{4+9+49}=\\sqrt{62}$\nAns. 62"
  }
